{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali","id":968070,"title":"alright, who bleached the drendali?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scarred Lands"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T12:19:18-07:00","id":968070,"title":"alright, who bleached the drendali?","content":"Dead God Trillogy book 1:<br /> &quot;An elf stepped into the attenuated column of light leaking down the hole, but not an elf of the kind Vladawen had once been, nor the afflicted sort he was now. This specimen\u2019s skin was dead black, and he carried a purplish geometric tattoo upon his brow.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> Scarred Lands Player's guide wrote:<br /> \u200b&quot;\u200bThey are tall and slender, with soft white hair and skin so pale as to make them seem almost albino. Their eyes, howeve are not those of an albino, but the same rich, lustrous blues, greens, golds, and violets of their surface elf cousins.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:58:09-07:00","id":968325,"title":"","content":"They may have done it to avoid the whole Drow blackface type of issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T00:12:43-07:00","id":968399,"title":"","content":"Are these guys subterranean? Pale makes a lot more sense, there's not much use for melanin underground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T02:48:04-07:00","id":968430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=968399#post968399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these guys subterranean? Pale makes a lot more sense, there's not much use for melanin underground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, they're subterranean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:14:03-07:00","id":968527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=968325#post968325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They may have done it to avoid the whole Drow blackface type of issue.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThat was my first thought too. I remember though, the offended sensibilities when the Forgotten Realms drow were 'redeemed' and became lighter skinned. So now that the drendali aren't 'always chaotic evil' I was wondering if they thought that through. Plus it's a frakking magic world. Underground = black skinned doesn't have to make sense. :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:28:33-07:00","id":968569,"title":"","content":"Since it's a magic world, does it matter? Is them having black skin that might look a bit too much like blackface so important?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:35:25-07:00","id":968609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Livewire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=968527#post968527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat was my first thought too. I remember though, the offended sensibilities when the Forgotten Realms drow were 'redeemed' and became lighter skinned. So now that the drendali aren't 'always chaotic evil' I was wondering if they thought that through. Plus it's a frakking magic world. Underground = black skinned doesn't have to make sense. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't remember so much offended sensbilities so much as it was stupid plotline that seemed forced which they seem to have competley retracted in 4th edition and 5th edition FR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:11:47-07:00","id":968695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=968609#post968609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't remember so much offended sensbilities so much as it was stupid plotline that seemed forced which they seem to have competley retracted in 4th edition and 5th edition FR.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, I can't find it, and I'm going from a grognard's memory. Attempting to find it leads to much whining how trying to look like a drow is racist or something. <br /> <br /> As I understood it people were complaining that the 'redeemed' drow were brown and the irredeemable drow were back (obsidian) skinned, indicating the dark skinned ones were evil and irredeemable. <br /> <br /> That said, I never read the books past the first part of the trilogy (and I liked Lisa Smedman's work). I never touched 4e and am glad if they've fixed that nonsense.<br /> <br /> I just don't se why they had the drendali 'lighten up'<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:35:43-07:00","id":969673,"title":"","content":"As I understand, the new edition is kind of a reboot, right? Why not take that as an opportunity to give the subterranean guys a skin tone that makes sense for creatures that are rarely if ever exposed to sunlight? Like, sure, it doesn't have to make sense because magic, but they had an opportunity to change it to make more sense from an evolutionary biology perspective, so they took it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:58:07-07:00","id":970002,"title":"","content":"The Drow's skin isn't black because they live underground, it black because they were punished by the Elven Gods.<br /> <br /> Its the black of someone dipped in spiritual tar, not the rich lovely brown of an African American. The white hair is a good metaphor for white feathers, the Drow have been banished and tarred and feathered for the crimes of their ancestors, which very unfair.<br /> <br /> But none of that has to my knowledge anything to do with The Scarred Lands, its Forgotten Realms info, so I see no reason these Dark Elves can't be Albinos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-15-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:40:49-07:00","id":970685,"title":"","content":"No arguing they can reboot all they want (Pathfinder elves are from another planet, and their drow are tainted by demons and Rovagug.) \u200bI'm just curious why the change.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:18:40-07:00","id":970871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Livewire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=970685#post970685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No arguing they can reboot all they want (Pathfinder elves are from another planet, and their drow are tainted by demons and Rovagug.) \u200bI'm just curious why the change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, because it actually makes sense from an evolutionary biology perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:27:04-07:00","id":970874,"title":"","content":"I wasn't involved in that part of the project, but I suspect the inconsistency is accidental. Scott and Stew would know for sure, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 09-16-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:40:32-07:00","id":970887,"title":"","content":"I woudln't be so sure that it is accidental. The new setting makes some effort to present good or evil being independent on the actual race or tribe, so I wouldn't be surprised that it is done on purpose.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I find it funny because I'm running a subterrean campaign in the Scarred Lands and I have placed a race of lizardmen who, after having lived down here for millenia, also have pale scales instead of green (or whatever color lizardmen typically have) ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T15:41:21-07:00","id":970948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=970871#post970871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, because it actually makes sense from an evolutionary biology perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bAre you speaking from a writer/developer/official capacity?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T15:44:42-07:00","id":970949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=970887#post970887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I woudln't be so sure that it is accidental. The new setting makes some effort to present good or evil being independent on the actual race or tribe, so I wouldn't be surprised that it is done on purpose.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I find it funny because I'm running a subterrean campaign in the Scarred Lands and I have placed a race of lizardmen who, after having lived down here for millenia, also have pale scales instead of green (or whatever color lizardmen typically have) ^^</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200b*nods* I do like that, it is a nice break away, allows for more nuanced canon. I just like my drendali dark skinned. I like the image.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:18:49-07:00","id":970969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Livewire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=970949#post970949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just like my drendali dark skinned. I like the image.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the best thing about fictional races used in role-playing games; they look however the GM describes them as looking when the player characters sight them.<br /> <br /> The various subterranean &quot;dark elves&quot; I've used have been pale-skinned for the entirety of my gaming career because Final Fantasy IV (back when it was labelled as II here in the states) and biology as I had learned it up to that point immediately outweighed what the D&amp;D books I picked up had to say (well, except for the D&amp;D products about the Shadow Elves of Mystara, since they were pale-skinned in every appearance other than the arcade beat-em-up games that Capcom made).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:56:05-07:00","id":970983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Livewire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=970948#post970948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> \u200bAre you speaking from a writer/developer/official capacity?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just seems like a logical assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:12:49-07:00","id":972585,"title":"","content":"It was me! I bleached the drendali. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As a couple folks have mentioned, it always made sense to me that a subterranean race would gradually become more pale, not darker-skinned. And since the drendali aren't supposed to be drow, whose skin color (at least in typical D&amp;D settings like the Forgotten Realms) is the result of a curse, I decided to revise their appearance. Dar'Tan is now the exception, his skin stained black by the shadow magic he practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12432-scott-holden","name":"Scott Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12432_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:53:25-07:00","id":972664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scott Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=972585#post972585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was me! I bleached the drendali. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As a couple folks have mentioned, it always made sense to me that a subterranean race would gradually become more pale, not darker-skinned. And since the drendali aren't supposed to be drow, whose skin color (at least in typical D&amp;D settings like the Forgotten Realms) is the result of a curse, I decided to revise their appearance. Dar'Tan is now the exception, his skin stained black by the shadow magic he practices.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThanks for the explanation Scott. That's what I was looking for. I disagree (after all, this is a game that breaks the laws of biology all the time) but I understand your reasoning. I just think jet black skinned elves look cool. :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:46:07-07:00","id":972741,"title":"","content":"No worries: In your game, you are the final arbiter. Your drendali can still be the old dark-skinned version!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12432-scott-holden","name":"Scott Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12432_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T20:07:53-08:00","id":1171698,"title":"","content":"No prob at all with them being pale honestly, but as an aside keeping Dar'tan dark-skinned and connecting it to his being Scarn's ultimate penumbral lord was a fun touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-03-2018, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T03:49:22-08:00","id":1179480,"title":"","content":"It's amusing to me that some elves seem to follow earth-human guidelines involving melanin, while the original Greyhawk elves were super-pale with light-colored hair and eyes, if they were gray elves, living high on mountain peaks, under constant sunlight, to middle-ranged Caucasian, for the high elves living in more or less normal human ranges of sunlight, to 'nut-brown' with darker hair and eyes, if living in the darkest depths of the forest, where sunlight rarely reached the ground, like the Grugach/'wild' elves, to dark greens and blues, for aquatic elves, living under the ocean, to pitch black, for dark elves, living in the sunless underground. Instead of getting darker in sunlight, and paler in shadows, elves went the exact opposite way, and got paler in sunlight, and darker in shadow (or bluer and greener if surrounded by water...).<br /> <br /> If there was an elven subrace in the plane of elemental fire (from Greyhawk, anyway, and perhaps Golarion, which seems to follow a similar paradigm), I imagine they'd eventually turn reddish in color, to match their surroundings.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T10:16:36-08:00","id":1181430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=1179480#post1179480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's amusing to me that some elves seem to follow earth-human guidelines involving melanin, while the original Greyhawk elves were super-pale with light-colored hair and eyes, if they were gray elves, living high on mountain peaks, under constant sunlight, to middle-ranged Caucasian, for the high elves living in more or less normal human ranges of sunlight, to 'nut-brown' with darker hair and eyes, if living in the darkest depths of the forest, where sunlight rarely reached the ground, like the Grugach/'wild' elves, to dark greens and blues, for aquatic elves, living under the ocean, to pitch black, for dark elves, living in the sunless underground. Instead of getting darker in sunlight, and paler in shadows, elves went the exact opposite way, and got paler in sunlight, and darker in shadow (or bluer and greener if surrounded by water...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Being far more familiar with old Mystara and later Kara-Tur, Dragonlance, Spelljammer, Forgotten and other settings, can't say i remember ever seing such a bit of setting/lore-building. Shadow Elves from Mystara were very much pale subterranean people (though the arcade games would give them a sort of violet skin tone that might or not have inspired the Drow, who knows).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=1179480#post1179480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was an elven subrace in the plane of elemental fire (from Greyhawk, anyway, and perhaps Golarion, which seems to follow a similar paradigm), I imagine they'd eventually turn reddish in color, to match their surroundings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Golarion playing with such a conceit i most certainly haven't heard about. Where does one find that, Elves of Golarion or some other book?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the reskining of the Drendali in the 2nd edition always sounded a move to take them away from the shadow of Drow pastiches with a partial homage to the Shadow Elves, D&amp;D's first subterranean elven antagonistic civilization, if memory tricks me not (and certainly might). I also find entertaining how this change makes Dar'Tan, who <b>does </b>have the look usually associated with Drow, into some sort of sorcerous freak, changed on a physical level by how long and deeply he has delved in his weird brand of shadow magics. Though i did say that before.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's good business if you're making a published setting to try to make your creations distinct from already classic/cliche/iconic takes of some sort of critter or gimmick, so no prob with that. One can always come up with cooky ideas involving shadow magic, developing ties to Dendrali (always thought it funny none were ever brought up considering how close their names and imagery can run) or other stuff of one's own to bring up a group of elven <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel/images/7/71/Ororo_Munroe_%28Terra-616%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20150313073317&amp;path-prefix=pt-br\" target=\"_blank\">Ororo</a> clones &amp; such if the urge comes up. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-01-2018, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T10:43:24-08:00","id":1181435,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> As an aside, nothing against elves, halflings, dwarves, humans, lizardfolk, ponypeople or whatever with unusual color arrangements from the primaries to outlandish combinations to drive birds-of-paradise into fits of envy. Fantasy settings should play with the fantastic, but exactly because of that i'm very much in favor of coming up with reasons - mythology is a thing and it is about crazy explanation for why the world and the beings upon it are or work in a certain way.<br /> <br /> For example, in a Pathfinder game i recently joined with some friends i introduced a group of people with the drow look - dark-blue to ebon-black skin, resplendent white hair, the whole nine yards. But they are <b>not </b>subterranean or even elven for that matter, coming from the dark side of the moon during certain astronomical alignements to explore, frolic, hunt or plunder according to the occasion and their fancy, their skin changes hues to make them more or less visible under the night sky and their manes will sometimes shimmer like ghostly flames the color of moonlight to confuse or scare the people of the land. when sunlight comes they either return though magic to their home or go to temporary hideouts in dungeons, mausoleums, ruins or subterraneans forts and manses captured from the Fallen World's true natives.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is - if you want color, <b>add </b>color, make something out of one's visual and conceptual choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-28-2020, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T09:25:54-07:00","id":1210051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=1181430#post1181430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being far more familiar with old Mystara and later Kara-Tur, Dragonlance, Spelljammer, Forgotten and other settings, can't say i remember ever seing such a bit of setting/lore-building. Shadow Elves from Mystara were very much pale subterranean people (though the arcade games would give them a sort of violet skin tone that might or not have inspired the Drow, who knows).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Golarion playing with such a conceit i most certainly haven't heard about. Where does one find that, Elves of Golarion or some other book?</b><br /> <br /> Anyway, the reskining of the Drendali in the 2nd edition always sounded a move to take them away from the shadow of Drow pastiches with a partial homage to the Shadow Elves, D&amp;D's first subterranean elven antagonistic civilization, if memory tricks me not (and certainly might). I also find entertaining how this change makes Dar'Tan, who <b>does </b>have the look usually associated with Drow, into some sort of sorcerous freak, changed on a physical level by how long and deeply he has delved in his weird brand of shadow magics. Though i did say that before.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's good business if you're making a published setting to try to make your creations distinct from already classic/cliche/iconic takes of some sort of critter or gimmick, so no prob with that. One can always come up with cooky ideas involving shadow magic, developing ties to Dendrali (always thought it funny none were ever brought up considering how close their names and imagery can run) or other stuff of one's own to bring up a group of elven <a href=\"http://&quot;https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/marvel/images/7/71/Ororo_Munroe_%28Terra-616%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20150313073317&amp;path-prefix=pt-br&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Ororo</a> clones &amp; such if the urge</div> </div> </div> </div>Talks about it in the Inner sea world guide and elves of golarion. Elves do have a kind of naturoethno chameleon thing going on where they become more like they're environment. There's aquatic elves with gills and blue skin and whatnot and there's snowcaster elves that live north and are ivory white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 04-23-2018, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T19:34:44-07:00","id":1210237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/968070-alright-who-bleached-the-drendali?p=1210051#post1210051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Talks about it in the Inner sea world guide and elves of golarion. Elves do have a kind of naturoethno chameleon thing going on where they become more like they're environment. There's aquatic elves with gills and blue skin and whatnot and there's snowcapped elves that live north and are ivory white.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know, must admit my knowledge of Golarion related pieces of lore is terribly, terribly slapdash, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}